BT /F2 8 Tf 1 1 1 rg 1 0 0 1 42 820 Tm (SAHAYAK | SIMPLE LANGUAGE GUIDE) Tj ET
BT /F2 18 Tf 0.04 0.16 0.32 rg 1 0 0 1 42 777.00 Tm (SAHAYAK Presentation Script) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 747.00 Tm (Three speakers: Shyamantika, Barakha and Himanxhu) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 726.00 Tm (Project: SAHAYAK - A Real-Time Indian Sign Language Recognition System) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 712.90 Tm (Lead developer and project head: Johan Jyoti Kuli) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 690.80 Tm (How to use this script) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 673.80 Tm (This guide gives each speaker a role, speaking lines, what to show and a handover to the next) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 661.70 Tm (    speaker. Practise the meaning rather than memorising every word. Check the camera, backend and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 649.60 Tm (    model before using the live website. Never claim an accuracy score unless a real test report) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 637.50 Tm (    supports it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 615.40 Tm (The project in one minute) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 598.40 Tm (SAHAYAK is a prototype that tries to recognize a limited set of trained signs and show their) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 586.30 Tm (    labels as text. It uses a browser camera, MediaPipe Hands, numeric hand features, a backend) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 574.20 Tm (    model and a website. Some extra features can translate text or speak it aloud.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 557.10 Tm (The static two-hand path uses 126 values. The continuous path uses 132 values per frame across 10) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 545.00 Tm (    time steps, making 1,320 values. The active labels can change, so check the live /api/status) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 532.90 Tm (    response before presenting. A label in a file alone does not prove the model recognizes it) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 520.80 Tm (    well.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 503.70 Tm (Say "prototype" and "supported signs." Do not say "complete ISL translator.") Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 481.60 Tm (Speaker 1 - Shyamantika Pegu) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.08 0.23 0.38 rg 1 0 0 1 42 461.60 Tm (Role: Introduction, Problem and Project Purpose) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 449.60 Tm (Suggested time: 1 minute 30 seconds) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 432.50 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 419.40 Tm (Good morning respected judges, teachers, and everyone here. We are presenting our project SAHAYAK,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 407.30 Tm (    a real-time Indian Sign Language recognition prototype.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 390.20 Tm (The word Sahayak means helper. We want to explore how a camera and a computer program could help) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 378.10 Tm (    show the name of a sign when someone may not understand that sign.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 361.00 Tm (Communication can be difficult when people do not understand the same language. Sign languages are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 348.90 Tm (    full languages with their own rules. Recognizing a few trained signs is not the same as) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 336.80 Tm (    understanding a full signed conversation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 319.70 Tm (Our aim is not to replace interpreters or claim that a computer can understand every ISL sentence.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 307.60 Tm (    We are building a prototype that recognizes a limited set of signs and displays the predicted) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 295.50 Tm (    label as text. The website also has extra speech and translation features.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 278.40 Tm (We will explain how it works, show the prototype and talk about its limits and future) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 266.30 Tm (    improvements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 249.20 Tm (Show: the homepage and project title.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 236.10 Tm (Handover: I have explained why we chose this problem. Barakha will now explain the system and how) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 224.00 Tm (    the recognition steps work.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.08 0.23 0.38 rg 1 0 0 1 42 203.90 Tm (Simple notes for Shyamantika) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 191.90 Tm (Computer vision means software that looks for useful information in images or video. A landmark is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 179.80 Tm (    a key point on a hand, such as a fingertip or joint. A feature is a number that describes the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 167.70 Tm (    hand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 150.60 Tm (If asked why this project matters, say it is a learning prototype and a starting point for testing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 138.50 Tm (    a possible accessibility tool.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 125.40 Tm (Do not say it recognizes every ISL sentence, that it is fully offline, or that it replaces an) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 113.30 Tm (    interpreter. Do not guess an accuracy percentage.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 91.20 Tm (Speaker 2 - Barakha Doley) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.08 0.23 0.38 rg 1 0 0 1 42 71.20 Tm (Role: System Design, Technology and Workflow) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 59.20 Tm (Suggested time: about 2 minutes) Tj ET
q 0.78 0.82 0.87 RG 42 44 m 553 44 l S Q
